---
<section id="work">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="label">Selected work</p>
        <h2>Four systems on AWS.</h2>
        <p>Each card shows its system running. Open one to see how it works, and the map above lights up its services.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="works">
      <article class="proj card" data-acc data-p="fee">
        <div class="art"><span class="idx">01</span><svg viewBox="0 0 390 250" role="img" aria-label="Animation: fee pages are scanned, normalised and totalled">
<rect class="scan" x="14" y="36" width="206" height="34" rx="9"/><g transform="translate(30,53)"><circle class="dotm" r="5"/><rect class="bar r1" x="16" y="-6" width="176" height="12" rx="6"/></g><g transform="translate(30,95)"><circle class="dotm" r="5"/><rect class="bar r2" x="16" y="-6" width="176" height="12" rx="6"/></g><g transform="translate(30,137)"><circle class="dotm" r="5"/><rect class="bar r3" x="16" y="-6" width="176" height="12" rx="6"/></g>
<text class="t" x="30" y="190">bank, remittance, fintech</text>
<g transform="translate(305,118)"><circle class="ringbg" r="46"/><circle class="ring" r="46" transform="rotate(-90)"/><text class="t" text-anchor="middle" y="4">real cost</text></g>
</svg></div>
        <div class="pcontent">
          <p class="pstat">In progress</p>
          <h3>FeePrint</h3>
          <p class="sum">Finds the real cost of sending or spending money.</p>
          <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pp-fee"><span>How it works</span><i class="chev"></i></button>
          <div class="accp" id="pp-fee"><div class="accin"><div class="pbody">
            <ul>
              <li><b>The problem.</b> Real costs are buried in bank, remittance and fintech pricing pages.</li>
              <li><b>What I'm building.</b> A platform that scrapes those pages, normalises the fees and calculates the true cost.</li>
              <li><b>How it holds up.</b> A Python pipeline with retries, timeouts and graceful failure handling. Infrastructure is in Terraform and ships through CI/CD. Precomputed fee data is served by low-latency APIs.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="flow"><span class="fn">Scraper pipeline</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">Normalise fees</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">Precomputed data</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">API, then React front end</span></div>
          </div></div></div>
          <div class="mets"><div class="met"><div class="big">IaC</div><p class="cap">all AWS infrastructure in Terraform</p></div><div class="met"><div class="big">CI/CD</div><p class="cap">every deploy goes through a pipeline</p></div></div>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">AWS</span><span class="chip">Terraform</span><span class="chip">Python</span><span class="chip">React</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="proj card" data-acc data-p="neuro">
        <div class="art"><span class="idx">02</span><svg viewBox="0 0 390 250" role="img" aria-label="Animation: a pull request moves through tests, image build and Lambda deploy">
<line class="trk" x1="30" y1="120" x2="360" y2="120"/>
<circle class="st st1" cx="80" cy="120" r="27"/><g transform="translate(80,120)"><path class="gl g1" d="M-9 1 L-3 7 L9 -7"/></g>
<circle class="st st2" cx="195" cy="120" r="27"/><g transform="translate(195,120)"><rect class="gl g2" x="-9" y="-9" width="18" height="18" rx="3"/></g>
<circle class="st st3" cx="310" cy="120" r="27"/><g transform="translate(310,120)"><text class="gt g3" text-anchor="middle" y="9">&#955;</text></g>
<text class="t" x="80" y="172" text-anchor="middle">tests</text><text class="t" x="195" y="172" text-anchor="middle">image</text><text class="t" x="310" y="172" text-anchor="middle">Lambda</text>
<text class="t" x="30" y="96" text-anchor="middle">PR</text>
<circle class="commit" cx="0" cy="120" r="7"/>
</svg></div>
        <div class="pcontent">
          <p class="pstat">Team project, 2025</p>
          <h3>NeuroGuide</h3>
          <p class="sum">A career platform for neurodiverse users, run as a container on Lambda.</p>
          <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pp-neuro"><span>How it works</span><i class="chev"></i></button>
          <div class="accp" id="pp-neuro"><div class="accin"><div class="pbody">
            <ul>
              <li><b>The product.</b> Gemini-powered job-description simplification, STAR interview prep, live speech coaching and ML job-fit scoring.</li>
              <li><b>Cold starts and ML dependencies.</b> Deployed the FastAPI back end as a Docker image on Amazon ECR, run by Lambda.</li>
              <li><b>Regressions.</b> A GitHub Actions pipeline runs Vitest, Playwright integration and end-to-end tests on every pull request.</li>
              <li><b>Security.</b> Least-privilege IAM roles in Terraform and strict CORS. EventBridge schedules the data refresh.</li>
              <li><b>Sync.</b> REST APIs and PostgreSQL models for cloud session sync, with debounced auto-save, conflict resolution and offline fallback.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="flow"><span class="fn">Pull request</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">GitHub Actions tests</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">Docker image in ECR</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">Lambda (FastAPI)</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">PostgreSQL</span></div>
          </div></div></div>
          <div class="mets"><div class="met"><div class="big" data-to="3">3</div><p class="cap">test layers on every pull request</p></div><div class="met"><div class="big">IAM</div><p class="cap">least-privilege roles in Terraform</p></div></div>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">Lambda</span><span class="chip">ECR</span><span class="chip">Terraform</span><span class="chip">GitHub Actions</span><span class="chip">FastAPI</span><span class="chip">PostgreSQL</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="proj card" data-acc data-p="bird">
        <div class="art"><span class="idx">03</span><svg viewBox="0 0 390 250" role="img" aria-label="Animation: a bird recording waveform is tagged, searched and retrieved">
<g class="wv"><rect x="30" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0s"/><rect x="41" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.3s"/><rect x="52" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.7s"/><rect x="63" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.2s"/><rect x="74" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.9s"/><rect x="85" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.5s"/><rect x="96" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.1s"/><rect x="107" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.8s"/><rect x="118" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.4s"/><rect x="129" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.6s"/><rect x="140" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.2s"/><rect x="151" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.9s"/><rect x="162" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.3s"/><rect x="173" y="78" width="6" height="64" rx="3" style="--d:-0.7s"/></g><path class="flowline" d="M200 110 C218 110 218 76 236 76"/><rect class="pill" x="236" y="62" width="118" height="28" rx="14" style="--d:0s"/><text class="pt" x="252" y="81">tag</text><path class="flowline" d="M200 110 C218 110 218 118 236 118"/><rect class="pill" x="236" y="104" width="118" height="28" rx="14" style="--d:1.2s"/><text class="pt" x="252" y="123">search</text><path class="flowline" d="M200 110 C218 110 218 160 236 160"/><rect class="pill" x="236" y="146" width="118" height="28" rx="14" style="--d:2.4s"/><text class="pt" x="252" y="165">retrieve</text>
<text class="t" x="30" y="205">recordings in S3, metadata in DynamoDB</text>
</svg></div>
        <div class="pcontent">
          <p class="pstat">Serverless, 2025</p>
          <h3>BirdTag</h3>
          <p class="sum">Tag and search bird recordings without managing a model server.</p>
          <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pp-bird"><span>How it works</span><i class="chev"></i></button>
          <div class="accp" id="pp-bird"><div class="accin"><div class="pbody">
            <ul>
              <li><b>The problem.</b> Wildlife researchers and citizen scientists managed bird observation recordings by hand.</li>
              <li><b>What I built.</b> A media platform to tag, search and retrieve recordings with metadata-driven queries.</li>
              <li><b>Architecture.</b> S3 for media, Cognito for sign-in, API Gateway with Lambda for metadata operations, and a DynamoDB schema for low-latency retrieval across large datasets.</li>
              <li><b>Inference without servers.</b> AI species-identification models packaged as ECR container images that Lambda consumes.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="flow"><span class="fn">Cognito sign-in</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">API Gateway</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">Lambda (+ ECR models)</span><span class="fa">&darr;</span><span class="fn">DynamoDB and S3</span></div>
          </div></div></div>
          <div class="mets"><div class="met"><div class="big">0</div><p class="cap">model servers to manage</p></div><div class="met"><div class="big" data-to="6">6</div><p class="cap">AWS services wired together</p></div></div>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">Lambda</span><span class="chip">S3</span><span class="chip">DynamoDB</span><span class="chip">Cognito</span><span class="chip">API Gateway</span><span class="chip">ECR</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="proj card" data-acc data-p="pose">
        <div class="art"><span class="idx">04</span><svg viewBox="0 0 390 250" role="img" aria-label="Animation: a moving figure drives load and more pods switch on">
<circle class="fig" cx="90" cy="62" r="11"/><line class="fig" x1="90" y1="73" x2="90" y2="125"/>
<line class="fig" x1="90" y1="125" x2="74" y2="170"/><line class="fig" x1="90" y1="125" x2="106" y2="170"/>
<g class="arm1"><line class="fig" x1="90" y1="86" x2="62" y2="112"/><circle class="jt" cx="62" cy="112" r="4.5"/></g>
<g class="arm2"><line class="fig" x1="90" y1="86" x2="118" y2="112"/><circle class="jt" cx="118" cy="112" r="4.5"/></g>
<circle class="jt" cx="90" cy="86" r="4.5"/><circle class="jt" cx="90" cy="125" r="4.5"/>
<rect class="pd" x="190" y="62" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk0"/><rect class="pd" x="230" y="62" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk1"/><rect class="pd" x="270" y="62" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk2"/><rect class="pd" x="310" y="62" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk3"/><rect class="pd" x="190" y="102" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk4"/><rect class="pd" x="230" y="102" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk5"/><rect class="pd" x="270" y="102" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk6"/><rect class="pd" x="310" y="102" width="30" height="30" rx="6" style="animation-name:pk7"/>
<rect class="meter" x="190" y="158" width="150" height="8" rx="4"/><rect class="mfill" x="190" y="158" width="150" height="8" rx="4"/>
<text class="t" x="190" y="150">load</text><text class="t" x="190" y="196">0.5 CPU, 512 MiB per pod</text>
</svg></div>
        <div class="pcontent">
          <p class="pstat">Containers, 2025</p>
          <h3>Pose Estimation</h3>
          <p class="sum">A pose detection API that runs inside 512 MiB and 0.5 CPU.</p>
          <button class="acc-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="pp-pose"><span>How it works</span><i class="chev"></i></button>
          <div class="accp" id="pp-pose"><div class="accin"><div class="pbody">
            <ul>
              <li><b>The brief.</b> Real-time movement analysis for fitness and physiotherapy apps, limited to 512 MiB of memory and 0.5 CPU per pod.</li>
              <li><b>Tuning.</b> Image resizing, garbage collection and concurrency control in the inference pipeline cut memory by 35% and doubled throughput.</li>
              <li><b>Scaling.</b> Docker on Kubernetes running on EC2 with horizontal pod autoscaling, load tested with Locust to mimic concurrent users.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="toy">
              <label for="users"><span>Concurrent users</span><span id="usersOut">120</span></label>
              <input id="users" type="range" min="0" max="400" step="10" value="120">
              <div class="pods" id="pods" aria-hidden="true"></div>
              <small id="podText"></small>
            </div>
          </div></div></div>
          <div class="mets"><div class="met"><div class="big" data-to="35" data-suf="%">35%</div><p class="cap">less memory per pod</p></div><div class="met"><div class="big" data-to="2" data-suf="x">2x</div><p class="cap">throughput across scaled pods</p></div></div>
          <div class="chips"><span class="chip">Kubernetes</span><span class="chip">EC2</span><span class="chip">Docker</span><span class="chip">FastAPI</span><span class="chip">YOLOv8</span><span class="chip">Locust</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>
      </div>

      <div class="also card">
        <p class="label">Also built</p>
        <h3>PantryPals, an Android app against food waste</h3>
        <p>Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Room and WorkManager. ML Kit barcode scanning and OCR read expiry dates, storage works offline first, and background alerts warn before food goes off.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
